                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "438ddcbc-c270-4c35-9237-4f5694bc462d",
                        "entry_id": "3857cbad-c63e-3cce-90c1-4877b0f7ee09",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "slenken"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bd41a6c9-0433-3b79-93a0-81da55a5ca6d",
                        "entry_id": "3857cbad-c63e-3cce-90c1-4877b0f7ee09",
                        "glosses": [
                            "greppel of slootje"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "22375178-32cb-4554-886f-0786cf6cc333",
                                "sense_id": "bd41a6c9-0433-3b79-93a0-81da55a5ca6d",
                                "text": "Via grenssluis `Ansitz' wordt van alles naar een slenk in het bos gesleept: 'een campingtafel, drie krukjes, tentdoek ter camouflage, koffieservies, gebak, dranken, een stuk reewild en een fazant ter overhandiging aan de IM-kandidate, een bordje met het opschrift HUBERTUSSCHENKE - GRENSBEREIK, telefoonverbinding naar beide beveiligingsposten."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "65f37f3a-39bc-37da-8e09-eddedef19e00",
                        "entry_id": "3857cbad-c63e-3cce-90c1-4877b0f7ee09",
                        "glosses": [
                            "een gedaald stuk aardkorst tussen twee verticale breukvlakken"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3f53b2bb-bb51-4f29-a488-5116e9e48258",
                                "sense_id": "65f37f3a-39bc-37da-8e09-eddedef19e00",
                                "text": "En platentektoniek, het op de wereldbol rondschuiven van de continenten, heeft er nog wat mee te maken ook: in Oost-Afrika, de streek waar beroemde fossielen als Lucy (Australopithecus afarensis) en latere hominiden zijn gevonden, scheurt zich een nieuwe continentale plaat los. En dat geeft vulkanisme. De scheur kennen we als de Grote Afrikaanse Slenk."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7c2a082f-952e-3b1f-a62e-98d0cec1b9f4",
                        "entry_id": "3857cbad-c63e-3cce-90c1-4877b0f7ee09",
                        "glosses": [
                            "een geul of rivierbedding waar eb- en vloedwater doorheen stroomt, zoals in Zeeland of het waddengebied."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e3715c63-cf51-4462-a474-213e157c723e",
                                "sense_id": "7c2a082f-952e-3b1f-a62e-98d0cec1b9f4",
                                "text": "⧖ Die slenk is nog als een smalle geul in het strand over en daarlangs ligt een smalle strook zeeklei; maar zij werd na 1880 aan de noordzijde dooreen zanddijk afgesloten, die nu tot een smal duin is aangestoven"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "83a4c64e-ea46-4838-bca5-d5b8dc480559",
                        "source_entry_id": "3857cbad-c63e-3cce-90c1-4877b0f7ee09",
                        "source_sense_id": "65f37f3a-39bc-37da-8e09-eddedef19e00",
                        "source_sense_description": "kloof",
                        "target_lang_word": "graben",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "graben",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1a399c83-1545-379f-87df-61640b97fab1",
                                        "entry_id": "d15cdc4c-1ce9-39d6-b7ed-e060ea5bb7b4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An elongated block of the Earth's crust, bounded by faults, that has dropped relative to the surrounding area."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a117595-da73-4847-bc58-7fddc9a29c49",
                                                "sense_id": "1a399c83-1545-379f-87df-61640b97fab1",
                                                "text": "1959, Robert G. Yates, George A. Thompson, Geology and Quicksilver Deposits of the Terlingua District, Texas, U. S. Geological Survey, Professional Paper 312, page 49,\nThe magnitude and shape of the large grabens strongly suggest that, when they formed, material much more mobile than ordinary rocks was present at a depth no greater than a few miles."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ddc7588-5c0e-417c-895d-2723b6939d5a",
                                                "sense_id": "1a399c83-1545-379f-87df-61640b97fab1",
                                                "text": "This system includes the Syrian and Lebanese grabens; the grabens of the Dead Sea, Wadi al Arabah, Gulfs of Aqaba and Suez, Red Sea, and Gulf of Aden; and the Ethiopian graben."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4bc6b88b-b811-4f3f-a35e-8b82e61dd538",
                                                "sense_id": "1a399c83-1545-379f-87df-61640b97fab1",
                                                "text": "1997, Jean-Marie Rouchy, 2: Paleogene Continental Rift System of Western Europe, Georges Busson, B. Charlotte Schreiber (editors), Sedimentary Deposition in Rift and Foreland Basins in France and Spain (Paleogene and Lower Neogene), page 83,\nMigration of the subsidence axis has been revealed by the detailed sedimentological studies in most of these grabens, particularly in the Bresse basin (Curial 1986; Moretto 1986/1987) and in Manosque-Forcalquier."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e0aa0ea-4ba6-4f63-96de-35f2a464b3af",
                                                "sense_id": "1a399c83-1545-379f-87df-61640b97fab1",
                                                "text": "2015, C. F. Burgess, et al., Chapter 35: The Structural and Stratigraphic Evolution of Lake Tanganyika: A Case Study of Continental Rifting, W. Manspeizer (editor), Triassic-Jurassic Rifting: Continental Breakup and the Origin of the Atlantic Ocean and Passive Margins, Part A, page 866,\nThese distinct zones of strike-slip or scissor faulting which separate adjacent half-grabens were termed interbasinal ridges and hinged highs by Rosendahl et al. (1986)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
